Jenkinsfile - Automating Your Builds as Code

Jenkinsfile is a simple text file (named `Jenkinsfile`) that you place right in your project's source code repository. This file contains the complete definition of your Jenkins pipeline – all the stages, steps, and actions needed to build, test, and deploy your software. 

What makes it special? 
- Version Control: Your pipeline is now tracked just like your application code. 
- Consistency: Every build uses the exact same defined process. 
- Collaboration: Teams can easily review, share, and improve the pipeline definition. 
- Reproducibility: Setting up new Jenkins jobs or even a new Jenkins server becomes incredibly simple.
